/-!
# MiniRust in Lean, and its correspondence with Anneal's MIR semantics

* `MiniRustSpec.Generated` (generated by `crates/anneal-minirust-gen` from the
  vendored, pinned MiniRust sources; never edited by hand): one Lean item per
  upstream Rust item, as a deep embedding of its syntax plus shallow Lean
  types for the spec's data types.
* `MiniRustSpec.Interp`: an executable interpretation of a small subset of the
  spec, transcribed by hand with quotations; `MiniRustSpec.Anchors` pins every
  transcribed upstream item to the generated model.
* `MiniRustSpec.Correspondence.*`: the correspondence between Anneal's MIR
  semantics (`Trusted.Rustc.V2026_06_01`) and that interpretation, with
  non-vacuity witnesses (`Correspondence.Witness`), witnesses for intrinsic
  calls that resolve to MIR fallback bodies (`Correspondence.IntrinsicFallback`),
  and boundary witnesses for the intrinsic constructs outside the fragment
  (`Correspondence.IntrinsicBoundary`).
* `MiniRustSpec.Audit`: fails the build unless the main theorems use only the
  standard axioms.

See `minirust/README.md`.
-/
